# suricataChecker – threshold.config for Suricata
# Location: C:\Program Files\Suricata\threshold.config (referenced from suricata.yaml)
#
# Suppresses false positive / too frequent alerts.
# The SID of an alert is shown in suricataChecker on the "EDR – Events" page (SID column).
# Suricata has to be restarted after a change (Settings -> Restart Suricata service, or Restart-Service Suricata).
#
# Syntax:
#   suppress gen_id <gid>, sig_id <sid>                                   – suppress completely
#   suppress gen_id <gid>, sig_id <sid>, track by_src, ip <IP/CIDR>       – suppress for a source
#   suppress gen_id <gid>, sig_id <sid>, track by_dst, ip <IP/CIDR>       – suppress for a destination
#   threshold gen_id <gid>, sig_id <sid>, type limit, track by_src, count <N>, seconds <S>
#                                                                         – max. N alerts in S seconds
#   rate_filter gen_id <gid>, sig_id <sid>, track by_rule, count <N>, seconds <S>, new_action alert, timeout <T>
#
# --- Active suppressions (noise of a host sensor on Windows) ---------------------
# LSO (Large Send Offload): outgoing packets captured before segmentation have length 0 in the IP header
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2200002
# Ethertype unknown to the decoder (Hyper-V / LLDP / proprietary L2 frames)
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2200121
# "Applayer Wrong direction first Data" – pcap on a Windows host captures outgoing TLS data
# before the handshake (packet order caused by offload), dozens of alerts a minute
suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2260001

# Examples (uncomment and adjust):
#
# An internal vulnerability scanner must not generate alerts:
# suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2001219, track by_src, ip 10.0.0.50
#
# At most 1 alert a minute per source for a noisy "INFO" signature:
# threshold gen_id 1, sig_id 2013028, type limit, track by_src, count 1, seconds 60
#
# Suppress an alert for the internal DNS server:
# suppress gen_id 1, sig_id 2027758, track by_dst, ip 10.0.0.1
